request: Items with due dates sort before items without.

single call 0: edit -> src/commands.ts, src/commands.test.ts  (Made `list` sort its visible todos with a stable `byDueFirst` comparator: todos that have a `due` come before those without, and the existing order is preserved within each group (Array.prototype.sort is stable). Sorting lives in `commands.list` alongside the existing done-filtering, so `formatList` stays a pure renderer and the `run` list command picks the behaviour up automatically. Added a test in commands.test.ts covering the mixed due/no-due case, verifying both groups' relative order.)
round 1: oracle GREEN
single call 1: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 11/11 tests pass). `list` now sorts todos with due dates before those without, using a stable comparator that preserves original order within each group; `formatList` remains a pure renderer and the `run` list command inherits the behaviour. The new test verifies the mixed ordering.)

